  "sv_aggregation_note": "Both SV F1 columns aggregate per-file tuple counts (the 16 per-file precision, recall and intersection counts pooled, F1 taken once from the totals), never a cross-file set union, so a suite's raw and adjusted values sit on one basis. The union collapses tuples emitted from more than one input VCF of the same assembly (34 on GRCh37, 13,402 on GRCh38, read as perl_tuples minus perl_tuples_union in the reports) and is carried in the reports' *_union counts for cross-engine volume comparison only. Every exclusion removes tuples outside the intersection, so the adjusted intersection equals the raw intersection on both assemblies (326,507 on GRCh37, 1,091,052 on GRCh38, the intersection and adj_intersection columns of manuscript/data/f1_observations.csv).",
  "sv_cnv_tr_mask_note": "The <CNV:TR> representation divergence (sv_cnv_tr_literal_expansion) has a symmetric filter predicate in compare_sv_concordance.py (filter_cnv_tr_expansion_divergences): it pairs VEP's literal reading of a <CNV:TR> record, a whole-unit insertion at the run's end for a gain or a deletion ending at the run's last base for a loss, with vep-rs's symbolic reading of the same record and transcript (feature_elongation or feature_truncation), and excludes the pair from both sides when the two readings agree on every other term. It excludes 1,368 pairs on GRCh37 and 2,644 on GRCh38, all in 07_cnv_repeat, out of 1,368 and 2,644 swap pairs in the class, every pair of the class on both assemblies, so the class is fully masked. 07_cnv_repeat's per-VCF F1 moves from 0.936322 to 1.000000 (GRCh37) and from 0.923333 to 0.999969 (GRCh38).",
  "sv_ground_truth": "per-VCF Perl r115.2 cache_version 115 reference output (sv_per_vcf_r115.2_c115_tr_regen_20260920 on both assemblies, the GRCh37 half generated against the full-genome Ensembl GRCh37 cache), 16 VCFs per assembly (13 synthetic + 3 real-world), compared via compare_sv_concordance.py per-VCF pairing. The s07/s08 rows are the tuple-weighted per-VCF overall across all 16 VCFs and the s09/s10 rows the tuple-weighted overall across the 3 real-world VCFs only; neither is an arithmetic mean.",
